# Maximum size, in bytes, of the RELEASE build of crates/conv-wasm/pkg/conv_wasm_bg.wasm.
# Enforced by .github/scripts/check-wasm-size.sh, which CI runs on every PR.
#
# This number ships to every visitor on every page load, so it is treated as a reviewable
# number rather than an emergent one. Raising it is allowed and expected — each real format
# converter adds bytes — but it is a deliberate line in a diff, with the reason in the PR
# description, not something that drifts upward unnoticed over twenty merges.
#
# Current headroom: baseline JPEG support (`crates/conv-core/src/formats/image/jpeg.rs`) brought
# the release build to 252853 bytes (246.9 KB), up from 217611 bytes just before it (GIF). A real
# separable forward+inverse DCT, canonical Huffman construction on both the decode and encode
# sides (with the classic mincode/maxcode/valptr array-based decode structure, not a hash map —
# JPEG decode's hot loop runs per-coefficient, not once per file), plus four embedded standard
# Annex K tables (two quantization, two Huffman, each duplicated luma/chroma) account for most of
# it. Checked first (`cargo tree -p conv-wasm`, this ticket): the dependency tree is unchanged
# (conv-core, js-sys, wasm-bindgen, same as before) — the growth is entirely this new hand-rolled
# codec, not a transitive dependency. 290000 leaves ~15% headroom above that for now.
#
# Previous headroom note (WebP lossless/VP8L): brought the build to 202094 bytes, up from 154078
# just before it (BMP/QOI/PNG/ICO) — a from-scratch bit reader/writer, canonical Huffman
# construction on both the decode *and* encode sides (VP8L has no "stored block" escape hatch the
# way DEFLATE gave PNG), LZ77 backward-reference decoding with VP8L's own distance-mapping table,
# the color cache, the meta-prefix (entropy image) mechanism, and all four pixel transforms — see
# `crates/conv-core/src/formats/image/vp8l.rs`/`webp.rs` module docs.
#
# Before raising this again: check whether the growth is actually the format you added, or a
# transitive dependency you did not intend to ship (`cargo tree -p conv-wasm` and
# `wasm-pack build --release -- --features …`). Budget bumps that turn out to be an
# accidental dependency are the exact regression this file exists to catch.
290000
